## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design a privacy-aware, multi-region data pipeline with governance and testing in a realistic setting.

## Key Concepts
- Pub/Sub streaming
- Multi-tenant masking and isolation
- CMEK and DLP integration
- Data Catalog lineage
- Schema evolution and backfills
- Two-region resilience and audits

## Code Example
```javascript
// Dataflow DoFn: mask PII based on tenant policy
class MaskPII {
  process(record, ctx) {
    const policy = getPolicy(ctx.tenantId);
    return maskRecord(record, policy);
  }
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test end-to-end lineage accuracy? 
- How would you handle policy updates without downtime?

## Why This Is Asked

This question probes practical data quality governance in a high-volume, multi-tenant streaming pipeline on GCP. It requires integrating Data Catalog for contracts and lineage, Dataflow for real-time checks, per-tenant isolation in BigQuery, and a robust rollback/testing strategy with synthetic data and anomaly detection. It also assesses cost and latency trade-offs.

## Key Concepts

- Data contracts and lineage via Data Catalog
- Real-time quality gates in Dataflow (schema drift, null checks, ranges)
- Per-tenant isolation in BigQuery datasets
- 24h per-tenant rollback and testing strategies
- Quarantine vs drop and anomaly alerting

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo-code: Dataflow DoFn quality gate
class QualityGateDoFn extends DoFn {
  processElement(ctx) {
    const rec = JSON.parse(ctx.element);
    if (!validSchema(rec) || hasNulls(outFields(rec))) {
      quarantine(rec);
      return;
    }
    emit(rec);
  }
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you test a schema drift event across tenants without data leakage?
- What metrics and SLAs tie to 24h rollbacks and data contracts?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests experience designing scalable, governed data platforms with multi-tenant isolation, data contracts, and end-to-end lineage on GCP. It also probes handling late-arriving data, PII masking, and per-tenant rollback plans.

## Key Concepts
- Multi-tenant isolation in BigQuery with Authorized Views
- Data contracts and lineage via Data Catalog
- Ingestion-time PII masking with DLP
- Event-time processing and late-arrivals in Dataflow
- Cross-region replication and immutable audit logs
- Schema evolution and per-tenant rollback strategy

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo-code: ingest path with DLP masking before storage
const ingest = (record) => {
  const masked = dlp.maskPII(record);
  pubsub.publish(masked);
};
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test schema evolution across 300 tenants without downtime?
- What metrics and alerting would you implement for cross-region replication health?
